WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.025
Active Directory zones and
Kerberos-signed dynamic updates.

2
00:00:04.025 --> 00:00:07.025
Start with a correction to
the vendor's documentation.

3
00:00:07.025 --> 00:00:12.242
Infoblox's NIOS 9.1 page for generating
the keytab, the key file NIOS uses

4
00:00:12.242 --> 00:00:17.725
for Kerberos-signed updates, shows the
ktpass command with RC4 encryption.

5
00:00:17.725 --> 00:00:23.155
Microsoft's July 2026 security update
moved Kerberos RC4 protections into

6
00:00:23.155 --> 00:00:27.292
enforcement mode on domain
controllers, with no rollback,

7
00:00:27.292 --> 00:00:33.325
and Windows Server 2025 domain controllers
don't issue RC4 ticket-granting tickets.

8
00:00:33.325 --> 00:00:37.162
So generate the keytab with AES 256.

9
00:00:37.162 --> 00:00:42.188
Note that ktpass also resets the account's
password and increments its key version.

10
00:00:42.188 --> 00:00:47.823
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Book
08's default is that the locator zones

11
00:00:47.823 --> 00:00:53.038
stay on AD DNS, reached by forwarding,
until the last domain controller goes.

12
00:00:53.038 --> 00:00:56.814
Under that default, NIOS
still needs AES keytabs,

13
00:00:56.814 --> 00:01:01.251
loaded in Phase 2, so that its
DHCP can send signed updates.

14
00:01:01.251 --> 00:01:06.158
One limit: an Infoblox DHCP server sends
signed updates for one domain only,

15
00:01:06.158 --> 00:01:09.325
though each member can
serve a different domain.

16
00:01:09.325 --> 00:01:11.037
Keys survive upgrades.

17
00:01:11.037 --> 00:01:15.024
The alternative is NIOS
hosting the AD zone itself.

18
00:01:15.024 --> 00:01:19.539
Allow transfers from the domain
controller, import the AES keytab,

19
00:01:19.539 --> 00:01:24.463
create the zone with the exact AD name,
import it, and allow signed updates.

20
00:01:24.463 --> 00:01:27.322
The wizard creates the underscore zones,

21
00:01:27.322 --> 00:01:30.601
such as underscore msdcs
and underscore sites.

22
00:01:30.601 --> 00:01:33.538
Then clear the option that
allows unsigned updates.

23
00:01:33.538 --> 00:01:38.580
But the Infoblox pages list
domain controllers up to 2016 on

24
00:01:38.580 --> 00:01:43.824
one page and 2022 on another, and
none names Windows Server 2025.

25
00:01:43.824 --> 00:01:46.250
Confirm support before you take this path.

26
00:01:46.250 --> 00:01:52.970
Sources: Infoblox NIOS 9.1.x Generating
the keytab file (Windows Server

27
00:01:52.970 --> 00:01:58.069
2016/2019/2022); Configuring
DNS for Active Directory;

28
00:01:58.069 --> 00:02:04.789
Configure Active Directory wizard;
About GSS-TSIG; Kerberos behavior;

29
00:02:04.789 --> 00:02:12.668
GSS-TSIG and upgrades; Microsoft Learn
Detect and remediate RC4 usage in Kerberos;

30
00:02:12.668 --> 00:02:18.980
Windows message center (July 2026
enforcement); Book 08, Chapter 04.
